{"abstract": [{"text": "iPhone, iPad, and Mac offer full-screen modes that let people expand a window to fill the screen, hiding system controls and providing a distraction-free environment.", "type": "text"}], "hierarchy": {"paths": [["doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/technologies", "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/human-interface-guidelines", "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/patterns"]]}, "identifier": {"interfaceLanguage": "swift", "url": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/going-full-screen"}, "kind": "article", "legalNotices": {"copyright": "Copyright &copy; 2026 Apple Inc. All rights reserved.", "privacyPolicy": "https://www.apple.com/privacy/privacy-policy", "termsOfUse": "https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/terms/site.html"}, "metadata": {"availableLanguages": ["en-US", "zh-CN", "ja-JP", "ko-KR"], "customMetadata": {"alert-date": "2025-06-09", "alert-text": "Updated guidance for hiding toolbars and navigation controls, and deferring Home Screen indicator gestures in full-screen iOS and iPadOS apps and games.", "supported-platforms": "ios,ipados,macos"}, "images": [{"identifier": "going-full-screen.svg", "type": "icon"}, {"identifier": "patterns-going-full-screen-thumbnail.png", "type": "card"}], "role": "article", "title": "Going full screen"}, "primaryContentSections": [{"content": [{"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "patterns-going-full-screen-intro.png", "type": "image"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"text": "Apple TV and Apple Watch don\u2019t offer full-screen modes because apps and games already fill the screen by default. Apple\u00a0Vision\u00a0Pro doesn\u2019t offer a full-screen mode because people can expand a window to fill more of their view or use the Digital Crown to hide passthrough and transition to a more immersive experience (for guidance, see ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/immersive-experiences", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": ").", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"anchor": "Best-practices", "level": 2, "text": "Best practices", "type": "heading"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Support full-screen mode when it makes sense for your experience.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " People appreciate full-screen mode when they want to concentrate on a task or be immersed in content. Consider offering a full-screen mode if your experience lets people play a game; view media like videos or photo slideshows; or perform an in-depth task that benefits from a distraction-free environment.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "If necessary, adjust your layout in full-screen mode, but don\u2019t programmatically resize your window.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " When a window is larger in full-screen mode than in non-full-screen mode, you want to keep essential content prominent while making good use of the extra space. For example, it might make sense to adjust the proportions of your interface without changing which items appear. If you make such adjustments, be sure they\u2019re subtle enough to maintain a consistent interface and avoid causing visually jarring transitions between modes.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Continue to provide access to essential features and controls so people can complete their task without exiting full-screen mode.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " For example, a full-screen media experience needs to make playback controls persistently available or easy to reveal when people need them.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Except in games, let people reveal the Dock while your iPadOS or macOS app is in full-screen mode.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " In iPadOS and macOS, it\u2019s important to preserve access to the Dock so people can quickly open other apps and Dock items. To help prevent people from accidentally revealing the Dock while they\u2019re playing your full-screen game, you can ask iPadOS to ignore an initial swipe up from the screen\u2019s bottom edge or hide the Dock entirely in macOS. For developer guidance, see ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/SwiftUI/UIHostingController/preferredScreenEdgesDeferringSystemGestures", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": " (SwiftUI), ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/UIKit/UIViewController/preferredScreenEdgesDeferringSystemGestures", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": " (UIKit) and ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/AppKit/NSApplication/PresentationOptions-swift.struct/hideDock", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": " (AppKit).", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "After people switch away from your full-screen experience, help them resume where they left off when they return.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " For example, a game or a slideshow needs to pause automatically when people leave the experience so they don\u2019t miss anything.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Let people choose when to exit full-screen mode.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " People generally don\u2019t expect full-screen mode to end automatically when they switch to a different experience or finish an absorbing activity, like playing a game or viewing a movie.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Prioritize content by temporarily hiding toolbars and navigation controls.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " You can offer a distraction-free environment by hiding elements when content is the primary focus, such as when viewing full-screen photos or reading a document. If you implement such behavior, let people restore the hidden elements with a familiar gesture or action like tapping, swiping down, or moving the cursor to the top of the screen. Be sure to keep controls visible when they\u2019re essential for navigation or performing tasks. Although a visionOS window can hide its toolbars or navigation controls, people generally expect different types of immersive experiences while wearing Apple\u00a0Vision\u00a0Pro; for guidance, see ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/immersive-experiences", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": ".", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"anchor": "Platform-considerations", "level": 2, "text": "Platform considerations", "type": "heading"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Not supported in tvOS, visionOS, or watchOS.", "type": "text"}], "type": "emphasis"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"anchor": "iOS-iPadOS", "level": 3, "text": "iOS, iPadOS", "type": "heading"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Consider deferring system gestures to prevent accidental exits in a full-screen app or game.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " By default, the Home Screen indicator automatically hides shortly after someone switches to your app or game. It reappears when someone interacts with the bottom portion of the screen, allowing them to swipe once to exit. Whenever possible, retain this behavior because it\u2019s familiar and what people expect. If supporting this results in unexpected exits, you can enable two swipes rather than one to exit. For developer guidance, see ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/SwiftUI/UIHostingController/preferredScreenEdgesDeferringSystemGestures", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": ".", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"anchor": "macOS", "level": 3, "text": "macOS", "type": "heading"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Use the system-provided full-screen experience.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": "", "type": "text"}, {"text": " ", "type": "text"}, {"text": "Using the system\u2019s full-screen support ensures that your full-screen window works well in all contexts. For example, some Mac models include a camera housing that occupies an area at the top-center of the screen. Using the system\u2019s full-screen support automatically accommodates this area. For developer guidance, see ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/AppKit/NSWindow/toggleFullScreen(_:)", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": ".", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "In a game, don\u2019t change the display mode when players go full screen.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " ", "type": "text"}, {"text": "People expect to be in control of their display mode, and changing it automatically doesn\u2019t improve performance.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"text": "For additional developer guidance, see ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/Metal/managing-your-game-window-for-metal-in-macos", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": ".", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Always let people choose when to enter full-screen mode.", "type": "text"}], "type": "strong"}, {"text": " ", "type": "text"}, {"text": "Prefer letting people use your window\u2019s Enter Full Screen button, View menu item, or the Control-Command-F keyboard shortcut. Avoid offering a custom menu of window modes. In a game, you might also provide a custom ", "type": "text"}, {"identifier": "https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/toggles", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": " that turns full-screen mode on and off.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"anchor": "Resources", "level": 2, "text": "Resources", "type": "heading"}, {"anchor": "Related", "level": 4, "text": "Related", "type": "heading"}, {"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/layout", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/multitasking", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/windows", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/the-menu-bar", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"anchor": "Developer-documentation", "level": 4, "text": "Developer documentation", "type": "heading"}, {"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/SwiftUI/View/fullScreenCover(item:onDismiss:content:)", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": " \u2014 SwiftUI", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/AppKit/NSScreen", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": " \u2014 AppKit", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/AppKit/NSWindow/CollectionBehavior-swift.struct", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": " \u2014 AppKit", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"inlineContent": [{"identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/Metal/managing-your-game-window-for-metal-in-macos", "isActive": true, "type": "reference"}, {"text": " \u2014 Swift, Objective-C", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}, {"anchor": "Videos", "level": 4, "text": "Videos", "type": "heading"}, {"items": ["doc://com.apple.documentation/videos/play/wwdc2025/208"], "style": "compactGrid", "type": "links"}, {"anchor": "Change-log", "level": 2, "text": "Change log", "type": "heading"}, {"header": "row", "rows": [[[{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Date", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}], [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Changes", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}]], [[{"inlineContent": [{"text": "June 9, 2025", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}], [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Updated guidance for hiding toolbars and navigation controls, and deferring Home Screen indicator gestures in full-screen iOS and iPadOS apps and games.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}]], [[{"inlineContent": [{"text": "June 10, 2024", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}], [{"inlineContent": [{"text": "Enhanced guidance for playing a game in full-screen mode.", "type": "text"}], "type": "paragraph"}]]], "type": "table"}], "kind": "content"}], "schemaVersion": {"major": 0, "minor": 3, "patch": 0}, "sections": [], "topicSectionsStyle": "compactGrid", "references": {"873F40BE-101A-4C0D-99F0-F5C7CE7B47A3": {"alt": null, "identifier": "873F40BE-101A-4C0D-99F0-F5C7CE7B47A3", "type": "image", "variants": [{"traits": ["1x"], "url": "https://devimages-cdn.apple.com/wwdc-services/images/3055294D-836B-4513-B7B0-0BC5666246B0/873F40BE-101A-4C0D-99F0-F5C7CE7B47A3/10046_wide_250x141_1x.jpg"}, {"traits": ["2x"], "url": "https://devimages-cdn.apple.com/wwdc-services/images/3055294D-836B-4513-B7B0-0BC5666246B0/873F40BE-101A-4C0D-99F0-F5C7CE7B47A3/10046_wide_250x141_2x.jpg"}, {"traits": ["3x"], "url": "https://devimages-cdn.apple.com/wwdc-services/images/3055294D-836B-4513-B7B0-0BC5666246B0/873F40BE-101A-4C0D-99F0-F5C7CE7B47A3/10046_wide_250x141_3x.jpg"}]}, "components-the-menu-bar-thumbnail.png": {"alt": "A stylized representation of the macOS menu bar displaying a selected menu. The image is tinted red to subtly reflect the red in the original six-color Apple logo.", "identifier": "components-the-menu-bar-thumbnail.png", "type": "image", "variants": [{"traits": ["2x", "light"], "url": "/images/com.apple.HIG/components-the-menu-bar-thumbnail@2x.png"}, {"traits": ["2x", "dark"], "url": "/images/com.apple.HIG/components-the-menu-bar-thumbnail~dark@2x.png"}]}, "components-windows-thumbnail.png": {"alt": "A stylized representation of a window with close, minimize, and full-screen buttons. The image is tinted red to subtly reflect the red in the original six-color Apple logo.", "identifier": "components-windows-thumbnail.png", "type": "image", "variants": [{"traits": ["2x", "light"], "url": "/images/com.apple.HIG/components-windows-thumbnail@2x.png"}, {"traits": ["2x", "dark"], "url": "/images/com.apple.HIG/components-windows-thumbnail~dark@2x.png"}]}, "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/immersive-experiences": {"abstract": [{"text": "In visionOS, you can design apps and games that extend beyond windows and volumes, immersing people in your content.", "type": "text"}], "identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/immersive-experiences", "images": [{"identifier": "immersive-experiences.svg", "type": "icon"}, {"identifier": "foundations-immersive-experiences-thumbnail.png", "type": "card"}], "kind": "article", "role": "article", "title": "Immersive experiences", "type": "topic", "url": "/design/human-interface-guidelines/immersive-experiences"}, "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/layout": {"abstract": [{"text": "A consistent layout that adapts across display sizes, orientations, and multitasking configurations helps people understand and enjoy your app or game on all their devices.", "type": "text"}], "identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/layout", "images": [{"identifier": "layout.svg", "type": "icon"}, {"identifier": "foundations-layout-thumbnail.png", "type": "card"}], "kind": "article", "role": "article", "title": "Layout", "type": "topic", "url": "/design/human-interface-guidelines/layout"}, "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/multitasking": {"abstract": [{"text": "Multitasking lets people switch quickly from one app to another, performing tasks in each.", "type": "text"}], "identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/multitasking", "images": [{"identifier": "multitasking.svg", "type": "icon"}, {"identifier": "patterns-multitasking-thumbnail.png", "type": "card"}], "kind": "article", "role": "article", "title": "Multitasking", "type": "topic", "url": "/design/human-interface-guidelines/multitasking"}, "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/patterns": {"abstract": [{"text": "Get design guidance for supporting common user actions, tasks, and experiences.", "type": "text"}], "identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/patterns", "images": [{"identifier": "overview.svg", "type": "icon"}, {"identifier": "patterns.png", "type": "card"}], "kind": "article", "role": "collectionGroup", "title": "Patterns", "type": "topic", "url": "/design/human-interface-guidelines/patterns"}, "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/the-menu-bar": {"abstract": [{"text": "On a Mac or an iPad, the menu bar at the top of the screen displays the top-level menus in your app or game.", "type": "text"}], "identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/the-menu-bar", "images": [{"identifier": "components-the-menu-bar-thumbnail.png", "type": "card"}], "kind": "article", "role": "article", "title": "The menu bar", "type": "topic", "url": "/design/human-interface-guidelines/the-menu-bar"}, "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/windows": {"abstract": [{"text": "A window presents UI views and components in your app or game.", "type": "text"}], "identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/Human-Interface-Guidelines/windows", "images": [{"identifier": "components-windows-thumbnail.png", "type": "card"}], "kind": "article", "role": "article", "title": "Windows", "type": "topic", "url": "/design/human-interface-guidelines/windows"}, "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/human-interface-guidelines": {"abstract": [{"text": "The HIG contains guidance and best practices that can help you design a", "type": "text"}, {"text": " ", "type": "text"}, {"text": "great experience for any Apple platform.", "type": "text"}], "identifier": "doc://com.apple.HIG/design/human-interface-guidelines", "images": [{"identifier": "human-interface-guidelines-page-image-card.png", "type": "card"}], "kind": "article", "role": "collection", "title": "Human Interface Guidelines", "type": "topic", "url": "/design/human-interface-guidelines"}, "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/AppKit/NSApplication/PresentationOptions-swift.struct/hideDock": {"abstract": [{"text": "The dock is entirely hidden and disabled.", "type": "text"}], "fragments": [{"kind": "keyword", "text": "static"}, {"kind": "text", "text": " "}, {"kind": "keyword", "text": "var"}, {"kind": "text", "text": " "}, {"kind": "identifier", "text": "hideDock"}, {"kind": "text", "text": ": "}, {"kind": "typeIdentifier", "preciseIdentifier": "c:objc(cs)NSApplication", "text": "NSApplication"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "."}, {"kind": "typeIdentifier", "preciseIdentifier": "c:@E@NSApplicationPresentationOptions", "text": "PresentationOptions"}], "identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/AppKit/NSApplication/PresentationOptions-swift.struct/hideDock", "kind": "symbol", "role": "symbol", "title": "hideDock", "type": "topic", "url": "/documentation/appkit/nsapplication/presentationoptions-swift.struct/hidedock"}, "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/AppKit/NSScreen": {"abstract": [{"text": "An object that describes the attributes of a computer\u2019s monitor or screen.", "type": "text"}], "fragments": [{"kind": "keyword", "text": "class"}, {"kind": "text", "text": " "}, {"kind": "identifier", "text": "NSScreen"}], "identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/AppKit/NSScreen", "kind": "symbol", "navigatorTitle": [{"kind": "identifier", "text": "NSScreen"}], "role": "symbol", "title": "NSScreen", "type": "topic", "url": "/documentation/appkit/nsscreen"}, "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/AppKit/NSWindow/CollectionBehavior-swift.struct": {"abstract": [{"text": "Window collection behaviors related to Mission Control, Spaces, and Stage Manager.", "type": "text"}], "fragments": [{"kind": "keyword", "text": "struct"}, {"kind": "text", "text": " "}, {"kind": "identifier", "text": "CollectionBehavior"}], "identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/AppKit/NSWindow/CollectionBehavior-swift.struct", "kind": "symbol", "navigatorTitle": [{"kind": "identifier", "text": "CollectionBehavior"}], "role": "symbol", "title": "NSWindow.CollectionBehavior", "type": "topic", "url": "/documentation/appkit/nswindow/collectionbehavior-swift.struct"}, "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/AppKit/NSWindow/toggleFullScreen(_:)": {"abstract": [{"text": "Takes the window into or out of fullscreen mode,", "type": "text"}], "fragments": [{"kind": "keyword", "text": "func"}, {"kind": "text", "text": " "}, {"kind": "identifier", "text": "toggleFullScreen"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "("}, {"kind": "keyword", "text": "Any"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "?)"}], "identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/AppKit/NSWindow/toggleFullScreen(_:)", "kind": "symbol", "role": "symbol", "title": "toggleFullScreen(_:)", "type": "topic", "url": "/documentation/appkit/nswindow/togglefullscreen(_:)"}, "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/Metal/managing-your-game-window-for-metal-in-macos": {"abstract": [{"text": "Set up a window and view for optimally displaying your Metal content.", "type": "text"}], "identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/Metal/managing-your-game-window-for-metal-in-macos", "kind": "article", "role": "article", "title": "Managing your game window for Metal in macOS", "type": "topic", "url": "/documentation/metal/managing-your-game-window-for-metal-in-macos"}, "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/SwiftUI/UIHostingController/preferredScreenEdgesDeferringSystemGestures": {"abstract": [{"text": "Sets the screen edge from which you want your gesture to take", "type": "text"}, {"text": " ", "type": "text"}, {"text": "precedence over the system gesture.", "type": "text"}], "fragments": [{"kind": "keyword", "text": "var"}, {"kind": "text", "text": " "}, {"kind": "identifier", "text": "preferredScreenEdgesDeferringSystemGestures"}, {"kind": "text", "text": ": "}, {"kind": "typeIdentifier", "preciseIdentifier": "c:@E@UIRectEdge", "text": "UIRectEdge"}], "identifier": "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/SwiftUI/UIHostingController/preferredScreenEdgesDeferringSystemGestures", "kind": "symbol", "role": "symbol", "title": "preferredScreenEdgesDeferringSystemGestures", "type": "topic", "url": "/documentation/swiftui/uihostingcontroller/preferredscreenedgesdeferringsystemgestures"}, "doc://com.apple.documentation/documentation/SwiftUI/View/fullScreenCover(item:onDismiss:content:)": {"abstract": [{"text": "Presents a modal view that covers as much of the screen as", "type": "text"}, {"text": " ", "type": "text"}, {"text": "possible using the binding you provide as a data source for the", "type": "text"}, {"text": " ", "type": "text"}, {"text": "sheet\u2019s content.", "type": "text"}], "fragments": [{"kind": "keyword", "text": "func"}, {"kind": "text", "text": " "}, {"kind": "identifier", "text": "fullScreenCover"}, {"kind": "text", "text": "<"}, {"kind": "genericParameter", "text": "Item"}, {"kind": "text", "text": ", "}, {"kind": "genericParameter", "text": "Content"}, {"kind": "text", "text": ">("}, {"kind": "externalParam", "text": "item"}, {"kind": "text", "text": ": "}, {"kind": "typeIdentifier", "preciseIdentifier": "s:7SwiftUI7BindingV", "tex